{1 = 1-12}
9=1.	Lady of all the divine powers, resplendent light, righteous woman clothed in radiance, 
15=2.	beloved of @wDN{An} and @wDN{Uraš}! Mistress of heaven, with the great diadem, 
19=3.	who loves the good headdress befitting the office of @fsux{en} priestess, 
23=4.	who has seized all seven of its divine powers! My lady, 
27=5.	you are the guardian of the great divine powers! You have taken up the divine powers, 
31=6.	you have hung the divine powers from your hand. You have gathered up the divine powers, 
35=7.	you have clasped the divine powers to your breast. 
39=8.	Like a dragon you have deposited venom on the foreign lands. 
43=9.	When like @wDN{Iškur} you roar at the earth, no vegetation can stand up to you. 
47=10.	As a flood descending upon (?) those foreign lands, 
51=11.	powerful one of heaven and earth, 
55=12.	you are their @wDN{Inana}. 

{13 = 13-19}
59=13.	Raining blazing fire down upon the Land, 
63=14.	endowed with divine powers by @wDN{An}, lady who rides upon a beast, 
67=15.	whose words are spoken at the holy command of @wDN{An}! 
71=16.	The great rites are yours: who can fathom them? 
75=17.	Destroyer of the foreign lands, you confer strength on the storm. 
79=18.	Beloved of @wDN{Enlil}, you have made awesome terror weigh upon the Land. 
83=19.	You stand at the service of @wDN{An's} commands. 

{20 = 20-33}
87=20.	At your battle-cry, my lady, the foreign lands bow low. 
91=21.	When humanity comes before you in awed silence at the terrifying radiance and tempest, 
95=22.	you grasp the most terrible of all the divine powers. 
99=23.	Because of you, the threshold of tears is opened, 
103=24.	and people walk along the path of the house of great lamentations. 
107=25.	In the van of battle, all is struck down before you. 
111=26.	With your strength, my lady, 
115=27.	teeth can crush flint. 
119=28.	You charge forward like a charging storm. 
123=29.	You roar with the roaring storm, 
127=30.	you continually thunder with @wDN{Iškur}. 
131=31.	You spread exhaustion with the stormwinds, 
135=32.	while your own feet remain tireless. 
139=33.	With the lamenting @fsux{balaŋ} drum a lament is struck up. 

{34 = 34-41}
143=34.	My lady, the great @wDN{Anuna} gods fly from you to the ruin mounds like scudding bats. 
147=35.	They dare not stand before your terrible gaze. 
151=36.	They dare not confront your terrible countenance. Who can cool your raging heart? 
158=37.	Your malevolent anger is too great to cool. 
162=38.	Lady, can your mood be soothed? Lady, 
166=39.	can your heart be gladdened? 
170=40.	Eldest daughter of @wDN{Suen}, 
174=41.	your rage cannot be cooled! 

{42 = 42-59}
