196=45.	and their people @varh[t4072.v5]{must drink it } @vart[t4072.v6,t4072.v5]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} could not drink }. They must lead their troops captive before you, 
203=46.	all together. They must scatter their élite regiments for you, 
207=47.	all together. 
211=48.	They must stand their able-bodied young men at your service, 
215=49.	all together. Tempests have filled the dancing-places of their cities. 
219=50.	They drive their young men before you as prisoners. 
223=51.	Your holy command has been spoken over the city which has not declared @q[city,Inana]{“The foreign lands are yours!”}, wherever they have not declared @q[,Inana]{“It is your own father's!”}; and it is brought back under your feet. 
227=52.	Responsible care is removed from its sheepfolds. 
231=53.	Its woman no longer speaks affectionately with her husband; 
235=54.	at dead of night she no longer takes counsel with him, 
239=55.	and she no longer reveals to him the pure thoughts of her heart. 
243=56.	Impetuous wild cow, 
247=57.	great daughter of @wDN{Suen}, 
251=58.	lady greater than @wDN{An}, 
255=59.	who can take anything from your province? 

{60 = 60-65}
259=60.	Great queen of queens, issue of a holy womb for righteous divine powers, 
263=61.	greater than your own mother, wise and sage, 
267=62.	lady of all the foreign lands, life-force of the teeming people: 
271=63.	I will recite your holy song! True goddess fit for divine powers, 
275=64.	your splendid utterances are magnificent. Deep-hearted, 
279=65.	good woman with a radiant heart, I will enumerate @varh[t4072.v7]{your divine powers } @vart[t4072.v8,t4072.v7]{@varn{2 mss. have instead:} good divine powers } @vart[t4072.v9,t4072.v7]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} holy divine powers } for you! 

{66 = 66-73}
288=66.	I, @wPN{En-ḫedu-ana} the @fsux{en} priestess, entered my holy @fsux{ŋipar} in your service. 
292=67.	I carried the ritual basket, and intoned the song of joy. 
296=68.	But @varh[t4072.v10]{funeral offerings were } @vart[t4072.v11,t4072.v10]{@varn{1 ms. has instead:} my ritual meal was } brought, as if I had never lived there. 
